        <h1>LeetCode 1872: Stone Game VIII (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Alice and Bob take turns (Alice first) on an array of stones. On each turn, a player picks an index i
                &gt; 0 and takes all stones from index 0 to i, scoring their prefix sum. Both play optimally to maximize
                or minimize the score difference (Alice maximizes, Bob minimizes). Return the score difference (Alice's
                score minus Bob's score).
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: stones = [-1,2,-3,4,-5]<br>
                Output: 5<br>
                Explanation: After converting to prefix sums [-1,1,-2,2,-3], Alice picks optimally and Bob counters,
                resulting in a score difference of 5.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int stoneGameVIII(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; stones) {
        for (int i = 1; i &lt; stones.size(); ++i) {
            stones[i] += stones[i - 1];
        }
        int result = stones.back();
        for (int i = stones.size() - 2; i &gt;= 1; --i) {
            result = max(result, stones[i] - result);
        }
        return result;
    }
};</code></pre>
